# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RideFlow environment configuration
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust the values for your setup.
# Never commit your real `.env` file — it is already gitignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port for the Express backend (REST API + static landing page).
# Defaults to 5000 if unset.
PORT=5000

# URL the Expo frontend uses to reach the backend at runtime.
# For local development this is your machine + the backend port.
# In production, set this to your deployed backend host (no protocol),
# e.g. EXPO_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=api.yourdomain.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=localhost:5000

# ── Redis (primary data store) ───────────────────────────────
# The backend auto-starts a local Redis instance on 127.0.0.1:6379
# with append-only-file (AOF) persistence. No configuration is
# required for local development.
# To use an external/managed Redis, update the connection settings
# in `server/storage.ts`.

# ── Optional: PostgreSQL ─────────────────────────────────────
# The core app runs entirely on Redis and does NOT require Postgres.
# A Drizzle/pg layer is scaffolded for teams who want a relational
# store. Uncomment and set this only if you wire it up.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/rideflow

# ── Optional: session secret ─────────────────────────────────
# Reserved for future session/auth hardening. Use a long random
# string in production.
# SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-secret

# ── Payments ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Current checkout supports cash and manual M-Pesa/EcoCash proof
# submission. Do not put wallet PINs or customer secrets in this file.
#
# Live mobile-money collection requires a merchant account and provider
# credentials/webhooks from Vodacom M-Pesa or a licensed Lesotho PSP.
# Configure those only after the provider integration is implemented.
